 wood and  nothing more  instead the real evil originates from  the entity that dwells inside it only  known as majora  it is made obvious that this evil has  left the mask at the end of the game  having been defeated at the hands of  link the mask was reduced to a mere  shell of wood and fiber as it likely  once was before majora housed itself  inside  all seems well until you realize that oh  yeah  the zelda timeline isn't straightforward  now is it  the events of majira's mask are but one  of three possible outcomes  so what about the other two timelines  what fate befell termina and its people  in those  realities since we're dealing with time  travel and alternate realities it can  get confusing real quick so i'll try to  sum it up as briefly as i can  the entire premise of majora's mask and  its outcome is entirely made possible  due to four different variables  link the happy mask salesman skull kid  and  timing i firmly believe that the  salesman and skull kid are alive at the  beginning of all three timelines  the child timeline speaks for itself as  that is where majora's mask takes place  kid is practically immortal as he is  classified as a spirit  not only that but he is featured in the  ancient stories of termina so he already  visited termina a long time ago and  would likely travel back there again in  the future  the mask salesman is seen at the  celebration during ocarina of times  credits which takes place at the  beginning of the adult timeline and in  the downfall timeline we find an  incarnation of him  possibly a descendant who has set up  shop in labrena this leads me to believe  that he has also survived this outcome  and one additional reason which i will  mention later  the only one who isn't around in the  other timelines is the hero of time but  even if he was it would still be  unlikely that the events of majora would  have occurred  sure the masked salesman could have  potentially traveled to termina  somewhere in between link's child and  adult adventure while link was trapped  inside the sacred realm only to travel  back to hyrule in time for the  celebration at the end  even then it still would have been  highly unlikely that things would have  aligned the exact same way  the key which brings it all together is  timing in order for the events of  majira's mask to play out like it did  all three individuals would have to be  in the exact right place  at exactly the right time i think it's  safe to say that the happy mask salesman  was already on his way back to hyrule  when he was ambushed by the skull kid  since he could never have been in the  possession of the mask if he was still  on his way to termina in turn the skull  kid too would have to be in the lost  woods at that exact moment in order to  run into the salesman  we can see in some of the cutscenes that  skull kid spends a lot of time just  messing around in termina with his  newfound fairy companions  so it's not like he's always hanging  around in the lost woods had the  salesman arrived in termina one day  earlier or later the two may have never  even run into each other  a majora's mask with the evil still  inside would have been taken to hyrule  or wherever else the masked salesman was  heading next and lastly link  also would have to arrive at the right  moment in order to get caught up in the  events which ultimately leads him to  defeating majora and ridding the mask of  the evil presence  and this incarnation of link aka the  hero of time would have also been the  only hero to be able to defeat majora  as without the ocarina of time this task  would have been impossible  this begs the question since link never  traveled to termina in the adult and  downfall timeline does this mean termini  has been annihilated by the moon  in those realities i mean link wasn't  around to stop it right  well no probably not because as we just  illustrated the timing is  very delicate one single change in the  schedule of the mask salesman or that of  skull kid  would already be enough to completely  throw the alignments off so you see when  it comes to the fate of termina  it's actually not that relevant whether  or not the masked salesman did or did  not travel to termina in the other two  timelines  if he did then he could have  successfully taken the mask from termina  and brought it somewhere else without  running into trouble along the way  if he did not then the mask would have  remained in termina but it would have  never found its way into the hands of  skull kid since he took the mask from  the salesman not to mention that if the  masked salesman was the one who  originally broke the seal on majora it  would still to this day be sealed in  darkness somewhere perhaps for all  eternity  either way in both cases the evil would  still be inside the mask  but let's say he did let's say that no  matter the outcome in hyrule  at some point in time the happy mask  salesman will travel to termina to  search for the mask  given his obsession with rare masks  there is a big chance that he was  already aware of the legends surrounding  majora even when he was still in hyrule  and was always planning  to look for it someday the only thing  that differs is when he set off on his  quest  this could mean that in the other two  timelines the mask salesman never ran  into the skull kit because the timing of  events would have been so radically  different  and thus he managed to successfully get  the mask out of termina this would  explain the presence of the mask in a  link between worlds  without writing it off as a simple  easter egg a link between worlds also  happens to take place in the downfall  timeline  the only timeline aside from the child  branch where we find an incarnation of  the happy masked salesman i'm not going  to get into how the mask ultimately made  its way onto a wall in link's house  as that is a theory on its own but  hypothetically speaking  let's say that this is the real deal the  real majira's mask  and in the adult timeline the mask also  made its way into hyrule or some other  place outside termina at some point by  that definition the mask we find in  those timelines would still have the  evil entity inside it since the skull  kid never stole it and the hero of time  is non-existent and thus never faced  majora to begin with  if this is the case how come we don't  see moons crashing towards earth  chaos and armageddon why is hyrule  spared this fate altogether  in order to answer this question we need  to do some theorizing about majora as an  entity  and how its powers operate  the true origin of majora's mask where  it was sealed and who this mysterious  tribe was who used it are unknown  we also have no definitive answer as to  how the masked salesman came into its  possession in the first place  if he was the one who broke the seal on  the mask or if someone else did and the  salesman simply made a deal for it but  the fact that he states that he went  through great lengths to acquire it  hints that he might be the one who took  it from its seal  the only thing we can find in the game  related to majora's backstory is a  secret shrine in akana canyon  this place is filled with imagery  related to the mask and could very well  be the place where the rituals spoken of  in the ancient legends took place  but if this is also where the mask was  found and by who remains up in the air  there exist countless theories about it  and perhaps i will make a video about it  someday as i do have some ideas but  these are topics for another time what  we want to focus on is not necessarily  the mask itself but rather the entity  that dwells within  majora is described as more than just a  faceless evil hellbound on causing  destruction  it has all the traits of that of a deity  somehow bound to a physical object  the four giants link encounters in the  game are classified as guardian deities  and are sealed inside a mask-like object  by majora  additionally we have the fierce deity  mask which as the name suggests is set  to house an  unknown yet powerful deity so it's only  natural to assume that the same  characteristics of a deity trapped or  bound to a mask  also applies to majora it may seem  trivial but there is a good reason why  this matters  we know that the zelda team has derived  a lot of their ideas and symbolism from  shintoism by far the biggest religion in  japan with almost 80 percent of its  population putting its customs into  practice to some degree  the shinto religion is well known for  the worship of a wide array of spirits  guardian deities and gods known as kami  the aspects of kami are  very complicated as there's many  different types subgroups and all with  different traits  names and various degrees of power and  importance even the word kami can  already mean different things depending  on the context but to oversimplify  kami can be elements of the landscape  forces of nature as well as beings and  the qualities that these beings express  more importantly kami are not inherently  good or evil  as shintoism makes no distinction  between the two generally speaking they  can be nurturing and comforting when  respected  or become vengeful and destructive when  neglected  shinto followers also believe that the  kami are the ones who can either grant  blessings or  curses to a person as such they desire  to appease the kami to  quote stay on their good side kami must  be appeased in order to gain their favor  and avoid their wrath and failing to do  so can lead to catastrophic events  commonly in the form of natural  disasters  dying crops or curses in order to avoid  this the shinto practice sees a wide  array of rituals  revolving around appeasing these deities  even demons which are called oni  and kami are generally regarded as the  same thing  and they too can either bring blessings  or curses the fine line separating  demons and gods is further evident from  the fierce deity mask  an english link while wearing the mask  is mostly referred to as simply  fierce deity link however in japanese  his name is kishin rinku  kishin being a japanese word made up of  the characters ogre  and god and commonly translates to  fierce god  or wrathful deity with this information  in mind let's take a closer look at  majora according to the legend majira's  mask was involved  in all sorts of ominous rituals by an  ancient tribe until finally being  quote sealed in darkness out of fear of  misuse  this seems to suggest that majora was  always inherently evil and caused  so much trouble that the ancient ones  decided to rid themselves  of the mask but what if it was the other  way around what if just like the kami  majora was just an entity neither good  nor evil  the tribe are the ones responsible for  using its power for its own benefit  the quote trouble caused by majora  spoken of in the legends  may not have been its own doing but  rather one or more members of the tribe  who used it for malicious intent  then to prevent further misuse by some  of the tribe's members the mask was  sealed away or hidden in a dark place  somewhere  again kami are not good or evil a deity  simply acts upon that which his  worshippers feed into  what if the reason why majora turned  vengeful was not because of the rituals  but because the rituals  stopped majora's evil nature may be the  result of neglect  after hiding the mask away from the rest  of the world the ancient tribe who used  its power  disappeared for unknown reasons sealed  in darkness  forgotten and abandoned by its  worshippers the entity inside the mask  slowly turned  vengeful and by the time the mask is  rediscovered it releases its anger upon  the world without mercy  as soon as it latches itself onto skull  kid it starts turning nature against the  population of termina  poisoned waters endless winters polluted  seas and cursed lands and finally  armageddon we even see this motif of  what it means to be good or evil  reflected back onto the final act of the  game some of the lunar children found on  the moon right before the final boss  fight hint at this  uncertainty saying things like the right  thing  what is it i wonder if you do the right  thing  does it really make everybody happy  or let's play good guys and bad guys  i'll be the good guy  and you'll be the bad guy essentially  doing a role reversal and placing link  in the shoes of the bad guy  even though he has done nothing but to  help the people of termina  and ridding the land of majora's curses  and during the boss fight itself we see  the three stages of majora through its  different forms  it starts with just a mask nothing more  than an object  then comes majora's incarnation the  entity inside the mask  this form of majora is playful energetic  a bit  silly even if it wasn't part of the boss  fight i'd say it doesn't really look all  that malicious  but then finally we transitioned to the  final stage majora's wrath  the hate which had festered and built up  inside the deity for being neglected and  forgotten  finally breaks free longing for revenge  on the world around it  there is one final aspect i want to  cover about majora and one which will  make it more apparent where i'm going  with all this  another trait of the shinto kami is that  in some cases they are bound to a  specific group of people  location or element in a sense they have  boundaries or domains from which they  operate or exercise their influence  they are also not considered omnipotent  or even immortal  kami can in fact die and there are many  examples of this happening in shinto  legend  the locations where these kami are set  to reside are often indicated by what's  called a torii gate a man-made archway  meant to communicate that you are now  entering the domain  so to speak of a specific kami it also  often leads to a shrine devoted to said  deity  as such i firmly believe that majora's  power is either non-existent or at the  very least severely diminished outside  the borders of termina  and there are several indications of  this first is the fact that skull kid is  able to take the mask off when he's  inside the lost woods  something he never does once he is in  termina this indicates that skull kid  still has control over himself when he  resides in hyrule  it's apparent that skull kid likes to  mess with people the act of ambushing  the mask salesman is something he does  without the mask and seemingly on his  own volition the same thing goes for  stealing link's horse and ocarina you  can clearly see from his body language  and silly demeanor that this is still  skull kid behind the wheel  his actions although rude are not  necessarily evil  not only that but despite link's attempt  to lash out at him and take back his  ocarina  skull kid never attempts to fight back  instead resorting to a game of chase  but as soon as link falls down the hole  and enters the boundaries of termina  skull kid immediately uses the mask's  power to cast a curse on link  almost as if he was waiting to strike as  soon as link ventured into its domain  his tone and demeanor also promptly  shifting from that of a dimwitted  prankster to  outright militias from this moment on we  never see skull kid take off the mask  until the moment at the very end where  madura states that his puppet has  fulfilled its role  this could indicate that when the mask  resides in hyrule for instance  its powers are negligible at best since  majora is a deity belonging to the land  of termina  which finally brings us to breath of the  wild the fact that majora's mask shows  up as a usable quest item and not just a  little reference hanging on a wall  somewhere is  already quite interesting i do believe  that the inclusion of the mask  is canon something i already covered in  my video about misco the great bandit  in that video i suggested that all items  related to the misco dlc  are likely canon they were part of a  series of ancient artifacts holding  historical value which the royal family  had collected over the many years until  misko broke into the castle and stole  them away  i also made the case that some of these  have to be replicas and not the real  deal  as some of these items or apparel were  either destroyed or banished or  in other words couldn't possibly have  made their way into the game in their  original form what i didn't mention in  that video was that the description of  some of these items  actually seems to confirm this just look  at the way some of these items are  described the phantom armor  this helmet looks like the one day  referring to the armored phantoms  supposedly wore  mitna's helmet a helmet much like the  one mitna wore when she fought alongside  the hero of twilight  the wording here such as looks just like  and much like definitely suggests that  they are not the original  now let's take a look at the description  for majora's mask an airy mask  passed down from ancient times nowhere  does it seem to hint that it's a replica  in fact the opposite is true  it states that it has been passed down  from ancient times you  cannot pass something down from ancient  times if it's not the real deal  so assuming that this is indeed the real  mask  the million dollar question then remains  which timeline does it originate from  is it the harmless version from the  child timeline after the evil has left  the mask  or is it from one of the other two where  majora's evil presence  is potentially still inside it we  definitely see that the mask  still has power since it's able to fool  undead style enemies  the eyes also still glow how is that  possible if majora was no longer inside  it  wouldn't it be just a piece of wood and  nothing more if this is the real version  of the mask one where madura is still  inside  it should still be mostly harmless since  as stated before  it likely has no power here however if  someone would be stupid enough to bring  the 